>>
Rule 2 (input tensor is empty or only contains non-negative values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (last dimension of a tensor matches first dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 4 (list of ints used as dimensions/axes, all non-negative and valid for tensor shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : 0 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 6 (input tensor is not empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 7 (tensor dimensions should be valid)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= 0 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
